scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:724:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2005-77-1,commonlii-LKCA-2005-77,(2006) 1 Sri LR 313,LKCA,2005,When the District Judge made order that the intervenient' s remedy is to file a separate action and vindicate his rights. the dispute between the intervenient and the Public Trustee remains until it is finally decided,(1) When the District Judge made order that the intervenient' s remedy is to file a separate action and vindicate his rights. the dispute between the intervenient and the Public Trustee remains until it is finally decided. (2) Hence the order will not finally dispose of the matter in dispute. The said order is not a judgment with the meaning of section 754(5),SRC030-s754(5),none,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
