scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:923:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-1994-18-3,commonlii-LKSC-1994-18,(2002) 3 Sri LR 299,LKSC,1994,"In making an order, the court should not be unduly influenced by the plaintiff's lack of a prima facie case.","(1) The discretion of the court to order security for costs of the defendant under section 416 of the Civil Procedure Code should be exercised judicially and with reason; and the amount ordered should itself be reasonable. (2) Section 416 provides for ""security"" which is required to be furnished, in order to create a fund from which an order for costs made by the court could be satisfied, if such costs are not directly paid by the plaintiff. ""Incurred"" costs under the section means that amount of costs which the court may financially award, regardless of what the party may actually spend. (3) In making the order the court should not be unduly influenced by the view that the plaintiff did not have a prirna facie case or the absence of a valuation report annexed to the plaint. (4) In the instant case order for costs was unnecessary and premature in that firstly, the trial could well be concluded within a short time; secondly, at 300 the stage of the",SRC030-s416,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:941:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-1996-16-1,commonlii-LKSC-1996-16,(1997) 1 Sri LR 103,LKSC,1996,A conflict of claims between a widow and an executor may require the executor's claim to be preferred over the widow's claim.,"(1) The pleadings in the case disclosed a ""conflict of claims"" between the widow and the executor within the meaning of Section 523 of the Civil Procedure Code, in view of which the claim of the executor has to be preferred to that of the widow. The expression ""conflict of claims"" cannot be confined to a situation where there are opposing",SRC030-s523,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:942:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-1996-34-1,commonlii-LKSC-1996-34,(1997) 1 Sri LR 208,LKSC,1996,A specified heir can be substituted upon the death of an applicant for land acquisition under section 71 of the Finance Act No. 11 of 1963 as amended.,"Upon the death of an applicant for the acquisition of a land under section 71 of the Finance Act No. 11 of 1963 as amended, there can be substitution of a ""Specified heir"" viz. a person mentioned in Section 71(2)(a) - in the prescribed order of priority - as well as of a testate heir. Whether the",SRC028-s36,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
