scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:897:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-1998-3-1,commonlii-LKSC-1998-3,(1998) 2 Sri LR 105,LKSC,1998,The court's decision is based on section 2.,"1. Accordingly, in terms of section 2 (1) (a) a defendant is entitled to counterclaim for damages for wrongful arrest of a vessel where there was either mala fides or gross negligence which implies malice. Per Fernando, J. "". . . . the power of the court, consistently recognised and exercised over a long period of time to award damages for malicious arrest, is ancillary or incidental to its power to arrest a vessel, and can be exercised in the same proceedings. Such a claim for damages can be made without awaiting the termination of the proceedings."" 2. The High Court has the power to order the plaintiff to give security for the defendant's counter-claim for damages for malicious arrest. 106",SRC030-s654,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
