essary should be allowed to stand in the way of his intervening. Per Amaratunga, J. ""When a relevant case is cited to a judge, it is his duty to carefully consider it and decide whether the law laid down in that case is applicable to the case before him; if he decides that, that case has no",SRC030-s18,none,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
